# Docs-led migration

Source of truth: `docs/architecture/` and `docs/frontend/`. Do not invent a parallel plan.

## Before any migration coding

1. Read `docs/architecture/pre-implementation-checklist.md` and `docs/frontend/12-migration-plan.md`.
2. Block Next.js app creation and slice implementation until Critical checklist items are `DECIDED` or explicitly `ACCEPTED RISK`.
3. Prefer Plan Mode for gate-clearing, ADR work, and architecture slices.
4. When leading migration, follow `.cursor/skills/nextjs-migration/SKILL.md`.

## Locked (never override without explicit user approval)

- Visual style parity — no redesign (ADR-010).
- Preserve email/SMS templates under `src/lib/server/messaging/`; provider-agnostic contracts only.
- Withdraw Lovable packages, `/lovable/*` routes, secrets, and host coupling (ADR-009).
- Existing backend remains primary API; Next.js is not a backend replacement (ADR-006).
- Target: Next.js 16.3.x, React 19.2.x, TypeScript 6.0.x, Vercel + Node 24 LTS.

## Execution order

Follow dependency-aware slices in `docs/frontend/12-migration-plan.md`. Do not skip foundation/auth/messaging gates. Do not delete TanStack/Lovable code until production smoke + rollback window + explicit user approval.

## Multi-model / multi-agent

Multiple AI models are allowed. They must follow `docs/architecture/multi-agent-workflow.md`: one docs plan, one owner per overlapping path, slice-scoped work. Parallel agents start at **slice 5** (marketing/legal); optional non-colliding work is D-28 spike or auth email BFF — one domain owner per overlapping path.
